1
00:00:23,399 --> 00:00:23,920
Haizhu!

2
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:25,920
Haizhu!

3
00:00:28,399 --> 00:00:29,199
Liu Haizhu!

4
00:00:31,519 --> 00:00:32,359
Liu Haizhu!

5
00:00:33,899 --> 00:00:36,520
Why are you calling me right now?

6
00:00:37,460 --> 00:00:38,219
Liu Haizhu!

7
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:50,560
What's all this about?

8
00:00:50,659 --> 00:00:51,920
Wailing like a ghost so early in the morning!

9
00:00:52,359 --> 00:00:53,679
Can't I sleep a bit longer?

10
00:00:55,420 --> 00:00:55,939
What's wrong?

11
00:00:57,020 --> 00:00:57,399
Look.

12
00:01:03,840 --> 00:01:04,739
What the hell did they write?

13
00:01:04,959 --> 00:01:06,900
(You gifted me a peach, I repay with fine jade)

14
00:01:11,519 --> 00:01:13,859
Did our house get visited by a fairy?

15
00:01:21,379 --> 00:01:22,239
Shift's over!

16
00:01:24,959 --> 00:01:25,859
See you, Old Wang!

17
00:01:27,560 --> 00:01:28,500
Whose is this?

18
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:31,180
Whose?

19
00:01:32,079 --> 00:01:32,959
Who left this behind?

20
00:01:33,879 --> 00:01:34,439
Where'd everybody go?

21
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:36,219
Shift's over.

22
00:01:37,659 --> 00:01:38,980
D-Director Ma.

23
00:01:40,560 --> 00:01:42,219
Is this... is this yours?

24
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:44,379
Look how skinny you are.

25
00:01:45,140 --> 00:01:46,180
You need some good nourishment.

26
00:01:47,099 --> 00:01:48,319
This stuff is really nutritious.

27
00:01:48,739 --> 00:01:49,359
Sweet, too.

28
00:01:50,159 --> 00:01:51,260
Drink up, nice and sweet.

29
00:01:53,719 --> 00:01:54,200
This...

30
00:01:54,379 --> 00:01:54,780
Here.

31
00:01:55,299 --> 00:01:56,319
F-For me?

32
00:01:56,920 --> 00:01:57,680
Just for you.

33
00:02:01,680 --> 00:02:02,159
Well...

34
00:02:02,540 --> 00:02:04,219
I couldn't possibly accept this.

35
00:02:04,700 --> 00:02:05,840
The factory meals are pretty good.

36
00:02:05,959 --> 00:02:06,480
You keep it.

37
00:02:06,659 --> 00:02:07,040
Thank you, but— Zhou Meng,

38
00:02:07,180 --> 00:02:07,980
Hold on, wait a second.

39
00:02:08,680 --> 00:02:10,080
The factory meals are one thing.

40
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:11,699
This is from me personally.

41
00:02:12,659 --> 00:02:13,819
Didn't spend a dime of public money.

42
00:02:14,560 --> 00:02:15,680
No, no...

43
00:02:16,199 --> 00:02:16,879
Director Ma...

44
00:02:17,020 --> 00:02:18,259
Do you need something from me?

45
00:02:18,300 --> 00:02:19,879
If something's up, just tell me.

46
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:23,939
Well...

47
00:02:24,879 --> 00:02:25,800
I want to talk to you about work.

48
00:02:28,280 --> 00:02:29,460
Come on, let's talk in the car.

49
00:02:30,180 --> 00:02:30,699
No, no, no.

50
00:02:30,979 --> 00:02:31,520
Director Ma.

51
00:02:31,680 --> 00:02:32,539
I just cleaned up.

52
00:02:32,639 --> 00:02:34,460
Why don't we just talk down here?

53
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:37,080
All cleaned up? Even better.

54
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:38,460
Well, you see...

55
00:02:38,680 --> 00:02:39,780
The thing is...

56
00:02:40,539 --> 00:02:42,719
I want to learn how to drive.

57
00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:44,319
You're an experienced driver.

58
00:02:44,520 --> 00:02:45,219
Show me the ropes.

59
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:46,219
Get in.

60
00:02:47,979 --> 00:02:48,479
Wait...

61
00:02:49,500 --> 00:02:50,099
This...

62
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:02,919
This is the speedometer.

63
00:03:03,460 --> 00:03:04,539
This is the oil pressure gauge.

64
00:03:04,960 --> 00:03:05,900
This is the water temperature.

65
00:03:06,719 --> 00:03:07,620
This is the load gauge.

66
00:03:08,860 --> 00:03:10,039
Got... got all that?

67
00:03:12,360 --> 00:03:13,219
That's great.

68
00:03:17,300 --> 00:03:19,300
I mean, you're a great teacher.

69
00:03:20,659 --> 00:03:21,379
Look at this.

70
00:03:21,860 --> 00:03:23,000
Southern girls really are...

71
00:03:23,900 --> 00:03:26,099
so neat and refined.

72
00:03:26,919 --> 00:03:27,699
Director Ma,

73
00:03:28,520 --> 00:03:29,360
now that we're done with the lesson,

74
00:03:29,479 --> 00:03:31,259
why don't we step down and talk?

75
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:33,280
I still need to clean up here.

76
00:03:34,840 --> 00:03:35,400
No rush.

77
00:03:35,879 --> 00:03:37,719
There's something else I want to ask you.

78
00:03:39,180 --> 00:03:39,879
Tell me,

79
00:03:40,479 --> 00:03:42,240
you and Liu Haizhu from maintenance...

80
00:03:42,539 --> 00:03:43,520
are pretty close, aren't you?

81
00:03:46,060 --> 00:03:48,080
Weren't we going to talk about work?

82
00:03:50,219 --> 00:03:51,500
Life and work go hand in hand.

83
00:03:53,159 --> 00:03:54,560
I'm only looking out for you.

84
00:03:56,240 --> 00:03:57,580
You're a girl from the south,

85
00:03:58,139 --> 00:03:59,020
all alone with no family here.

86
00:03:59,500 --> 00:04:01,360
Without someone to back you in the factory,

87
00:04:02,560 --> 00:04:03,680
life will be tough.

88
00:04:05,919 --> 00:04:07,020
I'm doing just fine.

89
00:04:07,759 --> 00:04:09,319
I have two hands and two feet.

90
00:04:09,719 --> 00:04:10,599
I get by fine.

91
00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:12,360
That may be true,

92
00:04:12,840 --> 00:04:13,919
but there are plenty of things

93
00:04:14,439 --> 00:04:16,399
a girl like you can't handle alone.

94
00:04:18,699 --> 00:04:20,420
I'll be honest with you, Zhou Meng.

95
00:04:21,899 --> 00:04:22,600
You...

96
00:04:23,639 --> 00:04:25,699
give me this truly wonderful feeling.

97
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:29,379
What kind of feeling?

98
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:30,620
Just that kind...

99
00:04:31,160 --> 00:04:31,819
that makes

100
00:04:33,259 --> 00:04:34,699
my heart thump like crazy.

101
00:04:36,459 --> 00:04:37,579
Not to boast,

102
00:04:38,379 --> 00:04:39,899
but so many female comrades in the factory

103
00:04:40,259 --> 00:04:42,139
literally throw themselves at me.

104
00:04:42,879 --> 00:04:44,000
Did you ever see me give any of them a chance?

105
00:04:44,620 --> 00:04:46,339
I've kept myself pure all this time.

106
00:04:54,060 --> 00:04:55,399
Is that so?

107
00:04:56,740 --> 00:04:57,519
I see.

108
00:04:58,199 --> 00:04:58,680
Well,

109
00:04:59,939 --> 00:05:00,519
Director Ma,

110
00:05:01,939 --> 00:05:03,860
I'm just an ordinary driver.

111
00:05:05,279 --> 00:05:07,040
You're such a powerful, high-ranking man,

112
00:05:08,399 --> 00:05:10,279
you're really out of my league.

113
00:05:11,019 --> 00:05:12,100
As for your 'pure jade,'

114
00:05:12,379 --> 00:05:14,860
save it for the female comrades who need it.

115
00:05:15,300 --> 00:05:16,120
Well, if that's all— Zhou Meng!

116
00:05:16,220 --> 00:05:16,819
I'll be going now.

117
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:17,680
Wait, Zhou Meng!

118
00:05:17,839 --> 00:05:18,519
Thank you. Goodbye! Zhou Meng!

119
00:05:18,519 --> 00:05:19,019
Zhou Meng!

120
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:26,000
Came on too strong...

121
00:06:28,540 --> 00:06:30,339
Haizhu, what are you doing here?

122
00:06:31,060 --> 00:06:32,079
I came here just to wait for you.

123
00:06:35,879 --> 00:06:36,639
This is for you.

124
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:38,439
I'm really sorry about yesterday.

125
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:39,259
Whatever I promise you from now on,

126
00:06:39,279 --> 00:06:40,120
I'll definitely keep my word.

127
00:06:40,699 --> 00:06:42,120
I hope you can forgive me.

128
00:07:08,920 --> 00:07:09,540
Got it.

129
00:07:09,959 --> 00:07:11,420
Glad the coal issue is sorted out.

130
00:07:12,699 --> 00:07:13,680
The weather forecast was wrong, too.

131
00:07:13,759 --> 00:07:14,899
Brought an umbrella for nothing.

132
00:07:17,420 --> 00:07:18,139
Where's my bike?

133
00:07:19,439 --> 00:07:20,279
Where did my bicycle go?

134
00:07:21,300 --> 00:07:22,759
Wait, where did you park it just now?

135
00:07:23,160 --> 00:07:24,339
I parked it right here.

136
00:07:27,779 --> 00:07:29,459
Tough thugs in the West,

137
00:07:29,959 --> 00:07:31,759
thieves' den Lijiatun;

138
00:07:32,279 --> 00:07:34,019
barren hills breed rogues,

139
00:07:34,339 --> 00:07:36,220
foul waters spawn demons.

140
00:07:36,459 --> 00:07:38,259
Tough thugs in the West,

141
00:07:38,399 --> 00:07:40,160
thieves' den Lijiatun;

142
00:07:40,420 --> 00:07:42,139
barren hills breed rogues,

143
00:07:42,439 --> 00:07:44,160
foul waters spawn demons.

144
00:07:44,899 --> 00:07:46,459
All filled out, Comrade.

145
00:07:46,579 --> 00:07:47,860
What do we do next?

146
00:07:51,959 --> 00:07:52,920
All right, you're all set.

147
00:07:53,060 --> 00:07:53,879
Go on home and wait for news.

148
00:07:53,920 --> 00:07:54,439
Don't worry.

149
00:07:54,839 --> 00:07:55,899
Wait, wait for what news?

150
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:56,759
The bike was just stolen.

151
00:07:56,779 --> 00:07:58,139
If we chase after it now, we can definitely catch them!

152
00:07:58,920 --> 00:08:00,060
That's easy for you to say.

153
00:08:00,180 --> 00:08:00,959
Songliao is a huge place.

154
00:08:00,959 --> 00:08:02,480
We need clues before we can go after anyone.

155
00:08:02,519 --> 00:08:03,279
Besides,

156
00:08:03,379 --> 00:08:04,139
in a single day,

157
00:08:04,139 --> 00:08:05,980
we deal with more than just your stolen bike.

158
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,319
No, even the kids know:

159
00:08:07,480 --> 00:08:08,500
"Tough thugs in the West,

160
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:09,360
thieves' den Lijiatun."

161
00:08:09,500 --> 00:08:10,439
Let's just head straight there!

162
00:08:10,860 --> 00:08:12,660
That's just kids chanting rhymes.

163
00:08:12,680 --> 00:08:14,459
You can't treat it like an official directive.

164
00:08:14,459 --> 00:08:14,939
Right?

165
00:08:15,100 --> 00:08:15,879
Look here, young comrade.

166
00:08:19,339 --> 00:08:20,560
Solving cases requires evidence.

167
00:08:21,019 --> 00:08:22,579
We can't just take a local jingle

168
00:08:22,720 --> 00:08:23,560
and dispatch officers to round people up.

169
00:08:23,939 --> 00:08:24,339
Besides,

170
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:26,480
there are over a hundred families in Lijia Village.

171
00:08:26,899 --> 00:08:28,199
They can't all be thieves, can they?

172
00:08:28,959 --> 00:08:31,259
Are... are you guys just brushing us off?

173
00:08:31,360 --> 00:08:32,559
We never said we wouldn't handle it.

174
00:08:32,559 --> 00:08:33,240
I hear you.

175
00:08:33,379 --> 00:08:35,159
I said go home and wait for news.

176
00:08:35,159 --> 00:08:35,840
Wait for what?

177
00:08:35,960 --> 00:08:37,879
By then, they'll have ridden it past Shanhaiguan!

178
00:08:41,080 --> 00:08:41,700
Thanks.

179
00:08:44,220 --> 00:08:45,620
Come on, it's getting dark.

180
00:08:45,700 --> 00:08:46,840
Ride my bike home first.

181
00:08:46,899 --> 00:08:48,179
I'll figure something out for your bike.

182
00:08:48,399 --> 00:08:50,580
What... what can you possibly do?

183
00:08:50,840 --> 00:08:51,960
Don't you worry about it. Trust me.

184
00:08:52,740 --> 00:08:53,440
Leave it to me.

185
00:08:53,460 --> 00:08:54,059
Hurry on home now.

186
00:09:05,600 --> 00:09:07,019
Head west from Songliao City,

187
00:09:07,519 --> 00:09:08,960
cross the Song River and go 30 li,

188
00:09:09,720 --> 00:09:10,559
and you reach the Western Suburbs.

189
00:09:11,419 --> 00:09:12,480
That place out in the Western Suburbs,

190
00:09:12,779 --> 00:09:13,799
nobody usually goes there.

191
00:09:14,639 --> 00:09:15,779
They say there's a gang of thieves

192
00:09:16,279 --> 00:09:18,440
who make a living off petty crime.

193
00:09:18,840 --> 00:09:20,000
They don't listen to reason,

194
00:09:20,080 --> 00:09:21,799
and they fight like they have nothing to lose.

195
00:09:22,720 --> 00:09:24,000
But to me, right now,

196
00:09:24,360 --> 00:09:25,440
Zhou Meng losing her bike

197
00:09:25,779 --> 00:09:27,320
is bigger than anything in the world.

198
00:09:28,039 --> 00:09:29,559
Just me and an umbrella,

199
00:09:29,740 --> 00:09:31,379
I set off for the Western Suburbs.

200
00:10:37,399 --> 00:10:38,379
Wh-Who are you?

201
00:10:39,259 --> 00:10:40,440
Who... who are you?

202
00:10:44,379 --> 00:10:45,759
Th-This is my place!

203
00:10:50,740 --> 00:10:51,600
This is my bike!

204
00:10:58,799 --> 00:11:00,299
Bro Two! Lao Wu!

205
00:11:00,419 --> 00:11:01,120
Hurry up!

206
00:11:01,299 --> 00:11:02,120
There's a thief in the house!

207
00:11:02,139 --> 00:11:02,860
Hurry! Let go of me!

208
00:11:03,100 --> 00:11:04,100
Let go of me! Hands off!

209
00:11:06,440 --> 00:11:07,059
Hurry!

210
00:11:08,960 --> 00:11:09,919
Let go! Get over here!

211
00:12:25,960 --> 00:12:27,720
Don't let him walk out of Lijia Village alive!

212
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:28,860
Get him!

213
00:12:52,019 --> 00:12:52,639
I'm telling you,

214
00:12:53,200 --> 00:12:55,019
this... this is Li Laogunzi's turf!

215
00:12:56,480 --> 00:12:57,120
Who do you run with?

216
00:12:59,960 --> 00:13:01,000
Fuck who I run with!

217
00:13:03,059 --> 00:13:03,659
The bike,

218
00:13:05,139 --> 00:13:05,919
I'm taking it with me.

219
00:13:09,299 --> 00:13:10,419
Anyone else got a death wish?

220
00:13:12,440 --> 00:13:12,919
Bring it on!

221
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:28,320
Over a dozen of you

222
00:13:29,980 --> 00:13:30,580
cornered one guy,

223
00:13:31,899 --> 00:13:32,720
and you let him get away?

224
00:13:36,460 --> 00:13:37,519
Those hands of yours...

225
00:13:38,179 --> 00:13:39,860
You can steal bikes, but can't hold a guy?

226
00:13:41,200 --> 00:13:41,940
Might as well chop them off!

227
00:13:44,879 --> 00:13:45,259
Bro,

228
00:13:46,399 --> 00:13:47,419
that kid's crazy tough.

229
00:13:48,779 --> 00:13:49,980
He's strong as hell.

230
00:14:00,980 --> 00:14:02,299
Is he really that strong?

231
00:14:08,019 --> 00:14:08,779
Tomorrow morning,

232
00:14:09,759 --> 00:14:10,399
head into town with me.

233
00:14:10,639 --> 00:14:11,840
We're dragging that punk out.

234
00:14:19,919 --> 00:14:20,740
Brother Batian,

235
00:14:20,879 --> 00:14:22,340
here in Songliao,

236
00:14:23,100 --> 00:14:25,139
things have been peaceful for years.

237
00:14:25,919 --> 00:14:27,960
Everyone has their own living,

238
00:14:28,179 --> 00:14:29,620
and everyone walks their own path.

239
00:14:30,899 --> 00:14:32,120
Maybe I got it wrong,

240
00:14:32,639 --> 00:14:33,480
but why does it feel like

241
00:14:33,960 --> 00:14:34,940
lately you, Brother Batian,

242
00:14:34,940 --> 00:14:36,340
always want to change the rules?

243
00:14:36,940 --> 00:14:38,080
Got a problem, Boss Zhang?

244
00:14:39,340 --> 00:14:41,080
I thought you only cared about

245
00:14:41,100 --> 00:14:42,720
making a living off women's bellies.

246
00:14:43,700 --> 00:14:44,460
I didn't expect

247
00:14:44,779 --> 00:14:46,460
you'd want a hand in street business too.

248
00:14:53,820 --> 00:14:54,879
If you put it like that,

249
00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:56,080
I'm actually terrified.

250
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:06,019
I was only joking around.

251
00:15:06,539 --> 00:15:07,360
A guy like me, Zhang Haoran,

252
00:15:07,419 --> 00:15:08,980
is just an honest businessman.

253
00:15:09,700 --> 00:15:11,360
As long as blood from outside

254
00:15:11,720 --> 00:15:13,019
doesn't splatter into my joint,

255
00:15:13,759 --> 00:15:15,299
I won't give a damn about anything.

256
00:15:29,120 --> 00:15:29,820
Boss Zhang,

257
00:15:30,279 --> 00:15:32,440
I can't stomach your food,

258
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:34,919
and the dirty business you run,

259
00:15:34,980 --> 00:15:35,899
I can't stand the sight of.

260
00:15:36,940 --> 00:15:37,840
So as for your turf,

261
00:15:38,720 --> 00:15:39,580
I'm making it my business.

262
00:15:42,700 --> 00:15:43,620
Well, if that's the case,

263
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:46,480
we'll go our separate ways.

264
00:15:47,120 --> 00:15:48,419
Since there's nothing left to talk about.

265
00:15:48,899 --> 00:15:49,720
Oh, there's plenty to talk about.

266
00:15:51,159 --> 00:15:52,000
With our fists.
